{"questions":[{"question_id":"lv7v49r8","content":"<p>Number of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds present in ethylene molecule is respectively :</p>","chapter":"chemical-bonding-and-molecular-structure","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-5th-april-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 5th April Morning Shift","permalink":"pnumber-of-sigma-and-pi-bonds-present-in-ethylen-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-dnm9yztjjasywsp6","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>Number of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds present in ethylene molecule is respectively :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"3 and 1\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"5 and 1\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"4 and 1\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"5 and 2"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Let's analyze the bond structure in an ethylene molecule (C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>4</sub>) to determine the count of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds.\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Ethylene consists of two carbon atoms double-bonded to each other, with each carbon atom also bonded to two hydrogen atoms. Each single bond is a <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. The double bond between the carbon atoms is made up of one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond and one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Here's how the bonds break down:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\n<li>Each carbon-hydrogen bond is a <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Since there are four C-H bonds, we have 4 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds from C-H bonding.</li>\n\n<li>The carbon-carbon double bond consists of one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond and one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Thus, we have 1 additional <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond from the C=C double bond.</li>\n\n<li>Total <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds = 4 (from C-H) + 1 (from C=C) = 5.</li>\n\n<li>There is 1 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond present in the carbon-carbon double bond.</li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:<br>\n\n<p>Option B: 5 and 1</p></p>"},"hi":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"<p>एथिलीन अणु में <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> और <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बॉन्ड्स की संख्या क्रमशः है:</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"3 और 1\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"5 और 1\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"4 और 1\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"5 और 2"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>आइए एक एथिलीन अणु (C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>4</sub>) में बंध संरचना का विश्लेषण करें ताकि <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> और <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंधों की गणना निर्धारित की जा सके।\n\n</p>\n\n<p>एथिलीन में दो कार्बन परमाणु होते हैं जो एक दूसरे से द्विबंध द्वारा जुड़े होते हैं, और प्रत्येक कार्बन परमाणु दो हाइड्रोजन परमाणुओं से भी बंधित होता है। प्रत्येक एकल बंध एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध होता है। कार्बन परमाणुओं के बीच द्विबंध एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध और एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध से बना होता है। यहाँ बताया गया है कि बंध कैसे विभाजित होते हैं:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\n<li>प्रत्येक कार्बन-हाइड्रोजन बंध एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध है। चूंकि चार C-H बंध हैं, इसलिए हमारे पास C-H बंधन से 4 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध हैं।</li>\n\n<li>कार्बन-कार्बन द्विबंध एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध और एक <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध से बना है। इस प्रकार, हमारे पास C=C द्विबंध से 1 अतिरिक्त <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध है।</li>\n\n<li>कुल <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध = 4 (C-H से) + 1 (C=C से) = 5।</li>\n\n<li>कार्बन-कार्बन द्विबंध में 1 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> बंध उपस्थित है।</li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<p>इसलिए, सही विकल्प है:<br>\n\n<p>विकल्प B: 5 और 1</p></p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"covalent-and-co-ordinate-bond","type":"mcq","year":2024,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-5th-april-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"3 and 1\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"5 and 1\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"4 and 1\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"5 and 2"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>Let's analyze the bond structure in an ethylene molecule (C<sub>2</sub>H<sub>4</sub>) to determine the count of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds.\n\n</p>\n\n<p>Ethylene consists of two carbon atoms double-bonded to each other, with each carbon atom also bonded to two hydrogen atoms. Each single bond is a <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. The double bond between the carbon atoms is made up of one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond and one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Here's how the bonds break down:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\n<li>Each carbon-hydrogen bond is a <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Since there are four C-H bonds, we have 4 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds from C-H bonding.</li>\n\n<li>The carbon-carbon double bond consists of one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond and one <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond. Thus, we have 1 additional <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond from the C=C double bond.</li>\n\n<li>Total <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.294ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 572 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bonds = 4 (from C-H) + 1 (from C=C) = 5.</li>\n\n<li>There is 1 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> bond present in the carbon-carbon double bond.</li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<p>Therefore, the correct option is:<br>\n\n<p>Option B: 5 and 1</p></p>"}]}